# Working files. None of these are referenced by any served page — checked with
# a grep across every html/js/css before excluding them.
#
# Left in, the deploy uploads ~700 MB and fails outright: handover.zip alone is
# 153 MB, over Vercel's 100 MB per-file limit.

iar-lab

# generation scratch: masters, raw renders, graded sets, contact sheets
images/_*

# the client handover package — a deliverable, not part of the site
handover
handover.zip

# the originals from the client's Drive: 6000x4000 camera files
images/_orig
# the mark clips' video sources — the site now ships the keyed webp instead
assets/*.mp4

# previews written by iar-lab/fit.py, alongside whatever it checked
*-fit.jpg

# placket correction working set: 2k PNG masters, not served
placket-fixed
tmp-src

# Internal working documents. Nothing on the site links to a .md — checked with
# a grep across every html and js before adding this — but every one of them was
# being served: PENDING-FROM-CLIENT.md, LAUNCH.md and CONTENT.md all returned
# 200 on the live domain, which put the client's open commercial risks, our
# internal decisions and their unreleased copy one URL away from anybody.
*.md

# The button and cuff close-up masters: 162 MB of PNGs, one per cloth plus the
# drafts. The served frames are derived into images/set/<slug>/4-cuff.webp and
# 5-button.webp with their tiers, so nothing here is referenced by any page.
# Left in, they alone are larger than the entire rest of the deploy.
IAMRATAN-all-button-closeups
cuff-images
